# .gitignore for NEON-Data
#
# Principle: code, config and documentation are tracked. Data, figures,
# environments and secrets are not. NEON data is freely re-downloadable
# from the API, so committing it buys nothing and costs repository size
# forever (git keeps every version of every binary you ever add).
#
# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line
# like "*.csv   # data files" is read as a literal pattern and matches
# nothing. Every comment here is on its own line for that reason.
#
# To track something this file excludes, negate it explicitly, e.g.
#     !reference/ster_sensor_depths.csv
# Negation works for extension patterns but NOT for files inside an
# excluded directory: git will not descend into one. That is why the
# output directories below are written as "out/*" rather than "out/".
#
# To find out why a path is being ignored:
#     git check-ignore -v <path>


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Keep this section first and never relax it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.neon_token
# neon_token_source.py is the pattern NEON's own tutorial suggests
neon_token_source.py
*.pem
*.key
credentials
credentials.*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEON downloads: portal zips, monthly directories, stacked output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# monthly dirs, e.g. NEON.D10.STER.DP1.00041.001.2024-01.basic...
NEON.D*/
# portal bundle dirs, e.g. NEON_temp-soil/
NEON_*-*/
# neonutilities download and stacking targets
filesToStack*/
stackedFiles/
*.manifest.*.json
# supporting docs (which are actually zip archives despite the extension)
NEON.DOC.*.pdf
NEON.QSG.*.pdf


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data files of any kind
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.arrow
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.nc
*.nc4
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.7z
# NEON EML metadata files
*.xml
*.xlsx
*.xls


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figures and generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
out/*
!out/.gitkeep
output/*
!output/.gitkeep
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep
scratch/
tmp/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.pdf
*.eps
*.gif
*.mp4


